00:07:31.690 --> 00:07:35.229
When Coraline refuses to comply with The Other
Mother’s requests, she’s thrown into the

00:07:35.229 --> 00:07:38.210
dark space behind the mirror and locked away
there as punishment.

00:07:38.210 --> 00:07:41.160
It is here that she makes contact with the
ghost children.

00:07:41.160 --> 00:07:44.699
She reaches around the dark room until she
finds what seems to be a nose and lips.

00:07:44.699 --> 00:07:48.550
The tall girl warns her to keep her voice
down, since the Beldam may be listening.

00:07:48.550 --> 00:07:51.970
When they find out that Coraline is still
alive, they encourage her to flee, explaining

00:07:51.970 --> 00:07:55.900
that they’ve been trapped for a very long
time; a time beyond reckoning.

00:07:55.900 --> 00:07:59.440
The boy is the one to suggest the idea that
Coraline could try to win their souls back

00:07:59.440 --> 00:08:02.580
from The Beldam -- and they all explain to
her that they’d be unable to leave with

00:08:02.580 --> 00:08:04.110
her when The Beldam lets her out.

00:08:04.110 --> 00:08:06.870
“Now we belong to the dark and to the empty
places.

00:08:06.870 --> 00:08:08.919
The light would shrivel us, and burn.”

00:08:08.919 --> 00:08:13.140
As Coraline curls up to sleep in the dark,
damp area behind the mirror, one of the ghost

00:08:13.140 --> 00:08:16.880
children kisses her cheek and whispers an
important clue, telling her to look through

00:08:16.880 --> 00:08:17.880
the stone.

00:08:17.880 --> 00:08:21.509
This is a reference to the adder stone given
to Coraline by her neighbors, it possesses

00:08:21.509 --> 00:08:25.699
magical properties that will help her scan
the Other World for the location of the souls.

00:08:25.699 --> 00:08:28.930
Coraline tells The Other Mother about her
encounter with the kids and says she must

00:08:28.930 --> 00:08:32.829
be planning the same for her, to which she
responds that, “nobody sensible believes

00:08:32.829 --> 00:08:34.169
in ghosts anyway.”

00:08:34.169 --> 00:08:37.691
Coraline searches the entirety of the Beldam’s
world and finds the boy’s soul hidden in

00:08:37.691 --> 00:08:40.880
a toy chest, the Tall Ghost Girl’s soul
guarded by the other versions of Spink and

00:08:40.880 --> 00:08:45.490
Forcible and The Goth Ghost girl’s soul
protected by the rats in Mr. Bobo’s apartment.

00:08:45.490 --> 00:08:48.910
After finding the first, the Ghost Boy urges
her to hurry on to save the others, but after

00:08:48.910 --> 00:08:52.529
the second, The Tall Ghost girl wishes her
to flee while she still has her life.

00:08:52.529 --> 00:08:56.150
The Beldam tries to throw her off by giving
her the key to the empty flat, and the children

00:08:56.150 --> 00:08:59.700
try to warn her, saying that the Beldam does
not mean well, and they don’t believe she

00:08:59.700 --> 00:09:00.880
would try to help Coraline.

00:09:00.880 --> 00:09:01.880
They’re right.

00:09:01.880 --> 00:09:05.550
It’s a trap, but Coraline is able to escape
and with the help of The Cat, retrieve the

00:09:05.550 --> 00:09:06.580
final soul.

00:09:06.580 --> 00:09:09.790
The voice of the Goth Ghost Girl gives her
one more piece of advice.

00:09:09.790 --> 00:09:11.980
“She has lied to you.

00:09:11.980 --> 00:09:18.450
She will never give you up, now she has you. She will no more give any of us up than she can change her nature.”

00:09:18.450 --> 00:09:21.871
This leads to the big confrontation where
Coraline tricks the Other Mother into the

00:09:21.871 --> 00:09:25.630
opening the passageway between the two worlds
so that she can rescue her parents and escape,

00:09:25.630 --> 00:09:28.350
but the Beldam catches the door as she tries
to pull it shut.

00:09:28.350 --> 00:09:31.839
Coraline suddenly becomes aware of other people
in the corridor with her.

00:09:31.839 --> 00:09:35.170
Their hands move through her and she feels
their strength added to her own.

00:09:35.170 --> 00:09:39.120
The voices tell her to hold strong and pull
and with the added power she’s able to force

00:09:39.120 --> 00:09:41.990
the door shut, dismembering The Beldam’s
hand in the process.

00:09:41.990 --> 00:09:45.450
As she crosses back into her own world, the
wraiths disappear.

00:09:45.450 --> 00:09:49.260
Upon getting back to her room, she removes
the marbles from her pocket before going to

00:09:49.260 --> 00:09:50.260
sleep.

00:09:50.260 --> 00:09:53.240
That night she dreamt of a picnic with the
three children, who now had their human-like

00:09:53.240 --> 00:09:54.240
forms back.

00:09:54.240 --> 00:09:57.180
Perhaps rather than being ghosts, they were
now angels.

00:09:57.180 --> 00:09:59.980
After eating, they play games in the meadow,
before having dessert.

00:09:59.980 --> 00:10:04.220
Coraline thanks them all for coming, but knows
not all is well when a shadow crosses their

00:10:04.220 --> 00:10:05.220
faces.

00:10:05.220 --> 00:10:09.120
The kids thank her for saving them, but explain
that for her it isn’t over quite yet -- not

00:10:09.120 --> 00:10:13.029
until she’s defeated the hand of the Beldam
that continues to scuttle around in the real

00:10:13.029 --> 00:10:14.029
world.

00:10:14.029 --> 00:10:17.170
The Goth Ghost Girl’s explanation implies
that they may now move onto the afterlife,

00:10:17.170 --> 00:10:21.490
saying that they’ll now set out for uncharted
lands, and what comes after no one alive can

00:10:21.490 --> 00:10:22.490
say.

00:10:22.490 --> 00:10:25.620
But before moving on, they remind Coraline
that she already has the traits necessary

00:10:25.620 --> 00:10:28.880
to defeat the Beldam: to be wise, brave and
tricky.

00:10:28.880 --> 00:10:32.610
The Boy hugs her and tells her to take comfort
in the fact that she’s still alive.

00:10:32.610 --> 00:10:35.630
Which is not… that… reassuring.

00:10:35.630 --> 00:10:38.920
Especially coming from someone who got killed
by the thing she’s about to fight.

00:10:38.920 --> 00:10:41.900
The children move away from her to a wooden
bridge by a stream.

00:10:41.900 --> 00:10:44.899
They wave back at her before the dream goes
into darkness.

00:10:44.899 --> 00:10:48.260
When Coraline awakes, the marbles that had
contained the three souls are broken.

00:10:48.260 --> 00:10:50.250
Whatever had been inside when was gone.

00:10:50.250 --> 00:10:54.240
She places the fragments in a box before formulating
her plan for taking down her Other Mother

00:10:54.240 --> 00:10:55.529
once and for all.

00:10:55.529 --> 00:10:59.340
Typically in a horror story, a ghost has some
kind of unfinished business -- and the spirit

00:10:59.340 --> 00:11:03.019
sticks around and haunts someone or something
until it’s final scores are settled.

00:11:03.019 --> 00:11:06.840
However, it seems to me that these three kids
were unable to move onto the afterlife because

00:11:06.840 --> 00:11:10.209
they were no longer in possession of their
own souls, and they were needed in order to

00:11:10.209 --> 00:11:11.209
move on.

00:11:11.209 --> 00:11:14.639
They don’t seem to need to hang around until
Coraline avenged them by trapping their killer

00:11:14.639 --> 00:11:18.470
at the bottom of the well, though it is possible
that they were just so confident in Coraline’s

00:11:18.470 --> 00:11:21.339
abilities that they could go on knowing that
they’ve already given all the advice they

00:11:21.339 --> 00:11:24.089
can give, and that she would have no problem
finishing the job.

00:11:24.089 --> 00:11:27.930
If you want to hear about the histories of
other Coraline characters click that playlist

00:11:27.930 --> 00:11:31.250
on the left and drop me a comment about who
you’d like to see me cover next.

